  "text": "I'm so sorry to hear that, John. It sounds like you're carrying a heavy load right now. It's not just the work stress, but also the emotional weight of your mom's illness. It's amazing you're still standing, to be honest.\n\nYou know, I've been in tough spots like this before, and I want you to know that you're not alone. Sometimes, when we're feeling overwhelmed, it feels like we're drowning in our own problems. But here's the thing: you're not drowning. You're just swimming in really deep water right now.\n\nI want to share something with you that might help. When I was in a similar situation, I found that talking to someone who understood what it was like to be in the trenches helped a lot. It wasn't about fixing everything right then and there; it was about feeling seen and heard.\n\nIf you're comfortable with it, I'd like to share a personal experience that might resonate with you. It's about a time when I had to deal with a difficult manager, and it felt like they just weren't listening. It was a really tough spot, but what I learned from it was that sometimes, the only way to get through is to find someone who gets it, even if it's just for a moment.\n\nWould you like to hear that story? Sometimes, hearing that someone else has been in a similar place can make a big difference.",
